{
  "description": "A diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures the trained recommender through a stable compatibility interface and produces an interpretation prompt grounded in measured metrics and their definitions.",
  "motivation": "Support evidence-based model revisions while preserving the RecHarness benchmark, all four Amazon datasets, and the native simulator's recommendation requirements.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Inspect view.model as the actual trained module and adapt probes to any architecture changes. Batches contain (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors shaped B × L. Use only public interaction histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; unavailable review data and simulator traits must remain unobserved. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty real training users, five per category. Select models using macro-average validation HR@10 across all four categories. Preserve the prescribed splits, seeds, dataset routing, environment-based data directory, and matching predictor architecture.",
  "pseudocode": "Initialize DiagnosisProbe(view, device).\nFor each diagnostic batch:\n  Compute architecture-compatible representations and recommendation scores.\n  Accumulate supported measurements using observed data only.\nReturn {metrics, metric_definitions}.\nBuild diagnosis_interpreter_prompt from those measurements and definitions, explicitly identifying unavailable information.\nGenerate unseen-item recommendations for five training users per category.\nEvaluate candidate models using the fixed macro validation HR@10 protocol.",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Connects architecture-aware diagnostics with a constrained recommendation evaluation workflow.",
    "negative": "The description specifies an integration contract, without a new diagnostic algorithm or model."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "A consistent diagnostic interface can support systematic model revisions and comparisons across architectures.",
    "negative": "Its usefulness depends on probe quality; no improvement in recommendation accuracy is demonstrated."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interfaces, batch structure, and evaluation objective are explicit.",
    "negative": "Architecture-specific probes, full-catalog recommendation generation, and training–prediction consistency require careful integration."
  }
}
